H6600.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6599 (פִּתְגָּם);
a word, answer, letter or decree
KJV: answer, letter, matter, word.

H6601.definition:
a primitive root;
to open, i.e. be (causatively, make) roomy; usually figuratively (in a mental or moral sense) to be (causatively, make) simple or (in a sinister way) delude
KJV: allure, deceive, enlarge, entice, flatter, persuade, silly (one).

H6602.definition:
from H6601 (פָּתָה) and H410 (אֵל); enlarged of God;
Pethuel, an Israelite
KJV: Pethuel.

H6603.definition:
or פִּתֻּחַ ; passive participle of H6605 (פָּתַח);
sculpture (in low or high relief or even intaglio)
KJV: carved (work) (are, en-) grave(-ing, -n).

H6604.definition:
of foreign origin;
Pethor, a place in Mesopotamia
KJV: Pethor.

H6605.definition:
a primitive root;
to open wide (literally or figuratively); specifically, to loosen, begin, plough, carve
KJV: appear, break forth, draw (out), let go free, (en-) grave(-n), loose (self), (be, be set) open(-ing), put off, ungird, unstop, have vent.

H6606.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6605 (פָּתַח);
to open
KJV: open.

H6607.definition:
from H6605 (פָּתַח);
an opening (literally), i.e. door (gate) or entrance way
KJV: door, entering (in), entrance (-ry), gate, opening, place.

H6608.definition:
from H6605 (פָּתַח);
opening (figuratively) i.e. disclosure
KJV: entrance.

H6609.definition:
from H6605 (פָּתַח);
something opened, i.e. a drawn sword
KJV: drawn sword.

H6610.definition:
from H6605 (פָּתַח);
opening (the act)
KJV: open(-ing).

H6611.definition:
from H6605 (פָּתַח) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has opened;
Pethachjah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Pethakiah.

H6612.definition:
or פֶּתִי; or פְּתָאִי; from H6601 (פָּתָה);
silly (i.e. seducible)
KJV: foolish, simple(-icity, one).

H6613.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H6601 (פָּתָה);
open, i.e. (as noun) width
KJV: breadth.

H6614.definition:
