a mass of persons (or figuratively, things), especially reg. organized forwar (an army); by implication, a campaign, literally or figuratively (specifically, hardship, worship)
KJV: appointed time, ([phrase]) army, ([phrase]) battle, company, host, service, soldiers, waiting upon, war(-fare).

H6636.definition:
or (more correctly) צְבִיִּים; or צְבִיִּם; plural of H6643 (צְבִי); gazelles;
Tseboim or Tsebijim, a place in Palestine
