KJV: Zobebah.

H6638.definition:
a primitive root;
to amass, i.e. grow turgid; specifically, to array an army against
KJV: fight swell.

H6640.definition:
(Aramaic) from H6634 (צְבָא);
properly, will; concretely, an affair (as a matter of determination)
KJV: purpose.

H6641.definition:
passive participle of the same as H6648 (צֶבַע);
dyed (in stripes), i.e. the hyena
KJV: speckled.

H6642.definition:
a primitive root;
to grasp, i.e. hand out
