H6666.definition:
from H6663 (צָדַק);
rightness (abstractly), subjectively (rectitude), objectively (justice), morally (virtue) or figuratively (prosperity)
KJV: justice, moderately, right(-eous) (act, -ly, -ness).

H6667.definition:
or צִדְקִיָּהוּ; from H6664 (צֶדֶק) and H3050 (יָהּ); right of Jah;
Tsidkijah, the name of six Israelites
KJV: Zedekiah, Zidkijah.

H6668.definition:
a primitive root;
to glitter, i.e. be golden in color
KJV: [idiom] fine.

H6669.definition:
from H6668 (צָהַב);
golden in color
KJV: yellow.

H6670.definition:
a primitive root;
to gleam, i.e. (figuratively) be cheerful; by transference to sound clear (of various animal or human expressions)
KJV: bellow, cry aloud (out), lift up, neigh, rejoice, make to shine, shout.

H6672.definition:
from H6671 (צָהַר);
a light (i.e. window); dual double light, i.e. noon
KJV: midday, noon(-day, -tide), window.

H6673.definition:
or צָו; from H6680 (צָוָה);
an injunction
KJV: commandment, precept.

H6674.definition:
or צֹא; from an unused root meaning to issue;
soiled (as if excrementitious)
KJV: filthy.

H6675.definition:
or צֹאָה ; feminine of H6674 (צוֹא);
excrement; generally, dirt; figuratively, pollution
KJV: dung, filth(-iness). Marg. for H2716 (חֶרֶא).

H6676.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6677 (צַוָּאר)
{the back of the neck (as that on which burdens are bound)}
KJV: neck.

H6677.definition:
or צַוָּר; (Nehemiah 3:5), or צַוָּרֹןlemma צַוָּרן missing vowel, corrected to צַוָּרֹן; (Song of Solomon 4:9), or (feminine) צַוָּארָה; (Micah 2:3), intensively from H6696 (צוּר) in the sense of binding;
the back of the neck (as that on which burdens are bound)
KJV: neck.

H6678.definition:
