an abyss (of the sea)
KJV: deep.

H6684.definition:
a primitive root;
to cover over (the mouth), i.e. to fast
KJV: [idiom] at all, fast.

H6685.definition:
or צֹם; from H6684 (צוּם);
a fast
KJV: fast(-ing).

H6686.definition:
from H6819 (צָעַר); small;
Tsuar, an Israelite
KJV: Zuar.

H6687.definition:
a primitive root;
to overflow
KJV: (make to over-) flow, swim.

H6688.definition:
from H6687 (צוּף);
comb of honey (from dripping)
KJV: honeycomb.

H6689.definition:
or צוֹפַי; or צִיף; from H6688 (צוּף); honey-comb;
Tsuph or Tsophai or Tsiph, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Zophai, Zuph.

H6690.definition:
from an unused root meaning to expand, breadth;
Tsophach, an Israelite
KJV: Zophah.

H6691.definition:
from H6852 (צָפַר); departing;
Tsophar, a friend of Job
KJV: Zophar.

H6692.definition:
