properly, a cliff (or sharp rock, as compressed); generally, a rock or boulder; figuratively, a refuge; also an edge (as precipitous)
KJV: edge, [idiom] (mighty) God (one), rock, [idiom] sharp, stone, [idiom] strength, [idiom] strong. See also H1049 (בֵּית צוּר).

H6698.definition:
the same as H6697 (צוּר); rock;
Tsur, the name of a Midianite and of an Israelite
KJV: Zur.

H6699.definition:
feminine of H6697 (צוּר);
a rock (Job 28:10); also a form (as if pressed out)
KJV: form, rock.
